{
  "description": "Message schema validation (protocol.md section 4, security.md section 4). Each case names the 'schema' the 'frame' object is validated against and whether it is 'valid' or 'invalid' (with a 'reason'). Schemas: 'bmx1' (handshake message 1), 'envelope' (transport carrier), 'data'/'ack'/'nak'/'bye' (inner plaintext types). A conforming validator must agree on every verdict. Note: validators check structure, not the semantic value of 'reason' — an unrecognized reason string is accepted (forward-compatible, per the versioning rule in protocol.md section 8). Note also: there is deliberately no case pinning an EMPTY JSON array as an invalid 'routes'. PHP's json_decode(..., true) renders both [] and {} as an empty PHP array, so that implementation cannot tell them apart -- and does not need to, because both encode 'no routes'. A non-empty array is unambiguous and is pinned instead. Pinning what every implementation can actually distinguish, and recording where that line falls, beats a vector six ports pass by luck.",
